<title>FRANCE: New York top ex-Paris air cargo destination in Oct.</title>
<headline>New York top ex-Paris air cargo destination in Oct.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Paris airports authority, the Aeroports de Paris (ADP), said New York was the top export destination from Charles de Gaulle and Orly Airports last month, despite a strong decline in traffic on 1995 levels.</p>
<p>October 1996 Paris-New York air cargo volume totalled 3,062 tonnes, down 31.1 percent on the same month last year, ADP figures showed.</p>
<p>In second place, was Chicago, with 2,596 tonnes, an increase of 13.3 percent on October 1995.</p>
<p>Hong Kong was ranked third with 2,357 tonnes flown ex-Paris, up 11.9 percent on 1995 levels, ADP said.</p>
<p>The top ten ex-Paris air cargo destinations in October 1996 with percentage changes from October 1995 were:</p>
<p> 1  New York	  3,062 tonnes   down 31.1pct</p>
<p> 2  Chicago	   2,596 tonnes   up   13.3</p>
<p> 3  Hong Kong	 2,357 tonnes   up   11.9</p>
<p> 4  Tokyo	     2,177 tonnes   down 28.8</p>
<p> 5  Mexico City     1,160 tonnes   up   23.5</p>
<p> 6  Sao Paulo	 1,140 tonnes   up   26.7</p>
<p> 7  Los Angeles	 963 tonnes   down 10.0</p>
<p> 8  Montreal	    956 tonnes   down 16.6</p>
<p> 9  Miami		 850 tonnes   up   74.3</p>
<p> 10 Singapore	   741 tonnes   up   11.4</p>
<p>- Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+44 171 542 5017</p>
